-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">OT</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">644</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ὄναιο τοῦ γενναίου χάριν</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">bless thee</b> for thy noble spirit, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">OC</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1042</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"3\"><span class=\"lex-n\">3</span> <span class=\"lex-gram\">aor.</span> <span class=\"lex-gram\">part.</span> <span class=\"gk\">ὀνήμενος,</span> of those to whom (or of whom) one says <span class=\"gk\">ὄναιο (ὄναιτὀ,</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">blessed,</b> <span class=\"gk\">ἐσθλός μοι δοκεῖ εἶναι, ὀνήμενος</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Od.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2.33</span> </span>: for this sense of a <span class=\"lex-gram\">part.</span> cf. <span class=\"gk\">ἐπίτριπτος, οὐλόμενος.</span> </div></div>"}